                <pb facs="0044" n="32" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg32"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultation 3(A)/431: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-20T16:00:00-04:00">November 20, 1943—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>568. For Spaeth from Duggan. Department perceives no objection to your supporting
                    the formula and procedure suggested by the Brazilian and Venezuelan members
                    described in your 977, November 16, 4 p.m. This step would appear to be
                    consistent with more positive action, your 948 of November 8 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">5</hi>], the advisability of which the Department
                    desires to consider further. [Duggan.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
